+**Descriptions.** The PR body is a one-minute briefing, not a lab notebook, for a reviewer who has the diff. It says why the change exists, what it leaves out, what it could break, and how you proved it works. Write short, simple sentences with few identifiers, no walls of text. The body becomes the squash commit body, so keep that commit under about 40 lines. When the run has an intent at `<root>/.nstack/intents/<slug>.md`, the PR body is where it outlives the run, because the file never reaches a commit and the merge-back deletes it. `## Why` carries its **Problem**, `## Scope` its **Out of scope**, and `## Tradeoffs` the **Decisions** a reviewer would ask about. Use `##` headings, not bold lead-ins, in this order, and drop a section with nothing to say:
 
 - `## Why`: the problem and approach, 1–3 short sentences. No SHAs, rebase genealogy, or "based on main" preamble.
 - `## What changed`: 1–3 short bullets. Name a real symbol or path only when it carries the change. Name both sides of a rename or retarget.
